  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact EXACTLY as given, serialize it as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, persist the exact bytes as proposal_canon.json, then compute hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt) (with salt = f3cbc213ebea7e0ef65aa832e1555da067108eb4117d37ecbebbec4a343cd8fe). A third party can re-derive by hashing the same proposal_canon.json bytes to reproduce hProposal, concatenating hProposal bytes with the same salt, and hashing again to reproduce the provided seedHex; mechanical check: sha256sum proposal_canon.json must equal hProposal, and the final seed must equal seedHex."
